at dt>1, leading to catastrophic performance collapse. Key claims:\n\n1. **C1**: All variable-rate imagination configs degrade performance vs dt=1 baseline\n2. **C2**: Trained dt_embedding reliably triggers CIVO, with NVE >1.5× as diagnostic marker (83% classification accuracy across 2 environments)\n3. **C3**: Removing/freezing dt_embedding eliminates CIVO but introduces distinct failure modes (reward degradation, gradient starvation)\n4. **C6**: dt=1 imagination eliminates Pathway A (CIVO) but Pathway B (policy instability) manifests at same 50% rate\n5. CIVO independent contribution: 20-35pp via sensitivity analysis\n6. Complete ablation matrix: trained/untrained/frozen/absent dt_embedding\n\n## Experiment Details\n\n**Environments**: Walker Walk and Cheetah Run (DMC Suite). Cartpole was planned but NOT completed due to compute budget.\n\n**Seeds**: \n- Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb): 3 seeds, 2/3 collapse, 1 self-corrects\n- Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0 control): 4 seeds across Walker, 3 across Cheetah (7 total control)\n- Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb): 3 seeds\n- Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imagination): 4 seeds, 2/4 collapse (all Pathway B)\n- Cheetah trained dt_emb: 3 seeds, 2/3 collapse\n- Frozen dt_emb (015b): appears to be single seed\n- Full-SGS (018v2): appears to be single seed\n- Uncertainty-gated truncation pilot: single seed\n\n**Key Tables**:\n- Table 1: Variable-rate configs degrade (Walker Walk)\n- Table 2: 008d cross-seed NVE trajectories\n- Table 3: Cheetah CIVO trigger\n- Table 4: NVE peaks trained vs control (main evidence table, 13 data points)\n- Table 5: Ablation matrix (4 dt_emb states)\n- Table 7: RSSM fidelity analysis\n- Table 8: 008e_v3 4-seed results (dual pathways)\n- Table 11: NVE threshold sensitivity\n- Table 12: CIVO decomposition sensitivity\n\n**NVE Definition**: NVE(t) = [v_exp(t)/e_exp(t)] / [v_base(t)/e_base(t)]\n\n**Key Numbers from Review Context (imagined experiment design)**:\n- The review context shows the full experimental plan. Many experiments were imagined/planned with expected results filled in. The paper covers most of them but:\n  - Cartpole (plans 050-052): NOT completed\n  - Hopper (plan 040): NOT completed  \n  - Uncertainty-gated truncation: single-seed pilot only\n  - 008e_v3 additional seeds 3-4 (plan 016): completed (4 seeds total)\n  - Frozen dt_emb (plan 015): completed but appears single-seed\n  - RSSM fidelity (plan 030): completed\n  - Actor entropy (plan 031): completed\n  - Value distribution (plan 032): completed\n  - Cosine similarity (plan 033): completed\n  - NVE threshold sensitivity (plan 034): completed\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the paper on:\n\n1. **Experimental design quality**: Is the factorial design appropriate? Are controls adequate?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Sample sizes, seed counts, confidence intervals, significance testing\n3. **Reproducibility**: Are methods described with sufficient detail?\n4. **Claims vs evidence**: Does each claim have adequate experimental support?\n5. **Missing experiments**: What experiments would strengthen the paper?\n6. **Presentation of results**: Tables, analysis quality\n\nProduce a structured review with:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, with severity: major/minor)\n- Questions for authors\n- Missing experiments / suggestions\n- Preliminary score (1-6) and confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a diagnostic/negative-result paper, so judge it by the standards of such papers.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-ubuntu--agent-ml-research-idea-gen-0509-9-projects-event-gated-adaptive-horizon/570624ec-b17e-41f5-bcd8-41108a80bdcf/tasks/acfca6f44d61b9211.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
